# Cyber Threats

<div style="background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px; margin: 20px auto; max-width: 85%; box-sizing: border-box; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word;">
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>Cybersecurity Threat</strong> is any potential cause of harm to a computer system or network.</p>
</div>

#### System-level threats include malware, ransomware, weak default settings, or misconfigured file sharing. Attackers exploit technical vulnerabilities to gain control, disrupt access, or corrupt data.

#### AI may increase the speed or scale of these threats.


## 📝 To Do

#### Review the threat vocabulary below. If you have time, check out the activity levels for each threat.

<div style="background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #2196f3; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px">
      <strong>Malware</strong> is software designed to harm, disrupt, or gain unauthorized access to a system. <br><br><i>If you have time, explore the <a href='https://studio.code.org/courses/artificial-intelligence-foundations-v2-2025/units/5/lessons/2/levels/3 target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>activity</a> from the curriculum to learn more.</i>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #f3e5f5; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #9c27b0; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px">
      <strong>Ransomware</strong> is a type of malware that locks or encrypts files on a computer, then demands payment (often in money or cryptocurrency) to restore access. <br><br><i>If you have time, explore the <a href='https://studio.code.org/courses/artificial-intelligence-foundations-v2-2025/units/5/lessons/2/levels/4' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>activity</a> from the curriculum to learn more.</i>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #2196f3; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px">
      <strong>Misconfiguration</strong> is a mistake or oversight in system settings that makes it easier for attackers to gain access. These issues can happen accidentally or as a result of poor default settings that leave files or systems too open.<br><br><i>If you have time, explore the <a href='https://studio.code.org/courses/artificial-intelligence-foundations-v2-2025/units/5/lessons/2/levels/2' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>activity</a> from the curriculum to learn more.</i>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #f3e5f5; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #9c27b0; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px">
      <strong>Distributed Denial of Service (DDoS) attack</strong> happens when many devices flood a website or server with requests at the same time. This overwhelms the system, slows it down, or crashes it, preventing others from getting in. <br><br><i>If you have time, explore the <a href='https://studio.code.org/courses/artificial-intelligence-foundations-v2-2025/units/5/lessons/2/levels/1' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>activity</a> from the curriculum to learn more.</i>
</div>

<p style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #B7E0E5; display: inline-block;">🚀 Additional Teacher Resource: <a href='https://www.canva.com/design/DAGvNt-cbGk/1hBKgfCeiM1NKJX9WIX7Ag/view?utm_content=DAGvNt-cbGk&utm_campaign=designshare&utm_medium=link2&utm_source=uniquelinks&utlId=h4745770232#3' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>Cyber Threat Vocabulary</a></p>

<p style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block;">
    ➡️ These activities are from Lesson 2. You can find more details in the full <a href='https://studio.code.org/courses/artificial-intelligence-foundations-v2-2025/units/5/lessons/2' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>Lesson Plan</a>.
</p>

